Date: Fri, 9 Apr 93 16:29:01 CDT
From: eder@hsvaic.boeing.com (Dani Eder)
Subject: Extropian Priorities

Here is the way I look at the priorities.  I made a model of technology
progress and determined that the tech singularity is due about 2035 AD.
By that time computers should be powerful enough to assist humans in
greatly increasing the rate of progress.  By greatly increase, I mean
by a factor of 5-10 times what it is now.

In life extension research, we have seen the life expectancy increase
from 50 years in 1900 to 80 years now, mostly by reducing cuases of
death at early ages.  I have every expectation that the life expectancy
will continue to increase.  The first major improvement is coming
from anti-oxidants and caloric restriction.  The evidence will start
showing in this decade from people who started taking Vitamin C years
ago that they live longer.

Once progress in mdical research gets revved up in the singularity,
the life expectancy should increase by more than 1 year per year,
i.e. you have a good chance to live a long time (well over 100 years)
by today's standards.

So, for those of us who are under 40, we should take care of ourselves
to increase the chances of living to the 2030's, and that means taking
advantage of the best life extension techniques available at any given
time.  Those over 40 and under 50 have a chance to extend their
lives to 2035 (that would be 92 yrs old for a 50 year old today),
but they have a large chance of dying earlier, so making cryonics
arrangements is a high priority, with agressive life extension
also a high priority.

Dani Eder

